        "source_occurrence_id": null,
        "source_locator": null,
        "speaker_label": "வச",
        "page_provenance": [
          {"pdf_page": 9, "printed_page": 8}
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "english_text": "Maharani—the prince... both are living corpses. I need only laugh, and the throne itself is mine. One bewitching glance—and this whole realm lies at my feet! I am the queen of the Maharaja's love, girl! I need only will it—Vasantha Sena, queen! Her son Vasanthan, prince!",
        "mode": "prose-faithful",
        "notes": [
          "The source's boast builds through short escalating claims; the English keeps that cumulative theatrical rhythm.",
          "`உயிர்ப்பிணங்கள்` is retained literally as `living corpses` rather than softened."
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
